.page uptime 1 say how long the system has been running

# SYNOPSIS
*uptime* [*-p*]

# DESCRIPTION
`uptime` prints one line: the time of day, how long the system has been up, and the load averages (from `/proc/loadavg`). With `-p` it prints just the uptime in words, such as `up 1 hour, 12 minutes`.

# EXAMPLES
    uptime
    uptime -p

# SEE ALSO
date(1), top(1), free(1)
